From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 48/48] PC5: the %fs: access of 32-bit code whose FS repair didn't
 take is done by Wine (Wine patch 0935)

Patch 0928's repair of the FS base isn't always applied by the kernel:
falloutwHR.exe was repaired once in GetStdHandle, then faulted again and
again in RtlEnterCriticalSection (mov %fs:0x18,%eax) and crashed. When
the same fault comes again at once, the faulting MOV between a register
and a %fs: operand is now done on the 32-bit TEB by Wine's handler, and
the thread goes on.
